  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nThe coldest air of the season will move into the region going\ninto the weekend. Higher elevations of the mountains should \nbegin to mix with and change over to snow Thursday night. The\ntiming of this changeover will affect snow totals. Snowfall has\nbeen decreased slightly to allow for a later transition, but if\nan earlier transition is realized, then a couple of more inches\ncould be added to the storm total. A couple of short waves will\nmove across the area Thursday night, again Friday afternoon and\nevening, and Saturday, enhancing precipitation. Friday night \ninto Saturday, gusty winds and cold air advection will create \nupslope snow conditions, even though 850 mb temperatures are not\nquite in the ideal range. The combination of these events will\nallow for several inches of snow in the higher elevations of \nthe mountains. Boundary layer temperatures will remain marginal \nfor snow in the lowlands. If snow does occur in those locations,\nground temperatures should be too warm for any accumulations.",
